  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Transparencia y Responsabilidad Gubernamental</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transparency and Integrity  in the Public Sector Activity (TIA) Counterpart International</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(El Salvador):  .Corruption in El Salvador impairs governance and weakens public confidence in democratic institutions. To tackle these issues, the Transparency and Integrity activity (TIA) employs a supply and demand approach to increase civic pressure for accountability while assisting government institutions committed to fighting corruption. The IP&apos;s experience working in El Salvador on governance initiatives (including human rights) and partnering with government and CSOs in closing spaces uniquely suit it to implement TIA&apos;s envisioned approaches to strengthening democratic governance..With FY 2024 funds, TIA will implement ten Memoranda of Understanding with six national government institutions and four municipal governments by providing technical assistance for public integrity frameworks, supporting the implementation of anti-bribery management systems, strengthening whistleblowing channels, identifying and supporting opportunities for digital transformation, and providing capacity building for training of public servants. On the demand side, the activity will implement grants to support citizen-led transparency and accountability efforts, as well as independent media, universities, and think tanks interested in overseeing the public sector or promoting transparency measures. These groups are demonstrating resilience and collaboration despite a challenging political environment, championing transparency in the face of increasing constraints on access to information and closing civic space. The activity will also work to strengthen private sector engagement by including ethics, procurement, and compliance standards in their daily operations.By supporting both the demand for and supply of transparent governance, the activity supports ICS MO 1.1, &quot;Strengthen democratic institutions and human rights promoting the ability of competing voices to challenge ideas and present alternate views,&quot; and Pillar II of the RCS.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">La actividad promover&#xe1; dos objetivos principales: (1) mejorar la transparencia y la rendici&#xf3;n de cuentas del gobierno y el cumplimiento de las pol&#xed;ticas anticorrupci&#xf3;n; y (2) aumentar la presi&#xf3;n ciudadana y la supervisi&#xf3;n del gobierno para combatir la corrupci&#xf3;n.</narrative>
  </description>
